<p>Hello Kay-Jah,</p>

<p>My name is Ann Wells&nbsp;and I am the Red Cross Business Development Manager for Blood Services.&nbsp;Thank you so much for your interest in participating in the American Red Cross Blood Drive Program. &nbsp;<br />
<br />
We are always welcoming new blood program sponsors and are thankful you have reached out to us. &nbsp;It is important that the Red Cross has a sufficient blood supply on hand to meet the needs of patients every day and be prepared for emergencies of all types like that of Hurricanes Harvey and Irma.</p>

<p>Our Madison Campus has a sight called Youngblood in Union South where we are continuously looking for groups to host a drive. &nbsp;We ask that you promote your drive and recruit at least 30 donors. &nbsp;We could work on that immediately if you choose.<br />
<br />
If not at Youngblood, we can work to build your own drive. &nbsp;Building a successful blood drive takes a little time;&nbsp;approximately 10 weeks. The first step in building your own blood drive is to gauge interest of your organization and how many would consider donating blood.&nbsp; Could you conduct an Interest Survey (see attached) to gauge the level of interest in giving Life Saving Blood?&nbsp; We need about 25-30 people interested in donating blood in order to set up an initial blood drive.&nbsp; More than 30 is even better!&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>

<p>I have also included a guide on hosting a successful blood drive.&nbsp; This will give you an idea of what to expect and some great ideas on generating interest.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Let&#39;s talk! Looking forward to working with you and please let me know the results of your Interest Survey!</p>
Best Regards,<br />
Ann<br />
